; Leg BX -- both levers.  Cautious x block 1, the corner PA/PC/BK bound.
;
; If the two compose, this is the configuration that would ship, and it is
; the only leg that measures the combination rather than inferring it.
; Round 1 could not: its BK already carried an inert PX_CAU, so nothing in
; that round ever had host-side unprefixing on at all.
;
; The two changes pull rxpeak in OPPOSITE directions, which is the reason
; this corner cannot be predicted from the other three:
;
;   block 1     removes ~130us per wire byte of foreground CRC, so the
;               ring drains faster and rxpeak should FALL (BK: 2,630)
;   cautious    raises file bytes produced per wire byte, so the foreground
;               does more per byte drained and rxpeak should RISE
;
; So read rxfull first here, not cps.  If BX overflows the ring while BK
; does not, the pair is not shippable as a pair no matter what the cps
; says, and the ring is the thing to fix before either lever lands.

set line /dev/tty.usbserial-ABBFKXM1
set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 1
log packets s16aeBX.pkt
send rcvbx.dat
statistics
